Original commit body from a95d517:

Framework detection now scans up to 3 directory levels deep to find
dependency manifests in subdirectories. This enables AUTO mode to
detect frameworks in monorepos and non-standard layouts where manifests
aren't at the repo root (e.g., backend/pyproject.toml, frontend/package.json).

The 12.11 bakeoff experiment showed a 100% detection gap - AUTO mode
found 0 entrypoints while --frameworks all found 51, because repos like
full-stack-fastapi-template have pyproject.toml in backend/ subdirectory.

This change closes that gap by:
- Adding _find_manifest_files() helper for recursive file discovery
- Updating all _detect_*_frameworks() functions to use recursive scanning
- Skipping common non-project directories (node_modules, vendor, venv)
- Adding comprehensive tests for subdirectory detection
